    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0787" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.25112A/7–2044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-20T19:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 21—1:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1231. Decrees have been prepared by Chilean Government which provide for interim
                    intervention leading Axis spearhead firms pending <pb facs="0788" n="774"
                        xml:id="pg774"/> liquidation or forced transfer after 60 days. Secretary
                    Chilean Commission states major decree, detailing procedure, and two other
                    decrees, naming companies affected, already have been fully signed and early
                    promulgation anticipated. Reference my telegram 1189 July 10 and my A–509 July
                        10,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d736-f1"/> issuance these decrees would constitute
                    step toward accomplishment of desired local controls program which would justify
                    publication accumulated deletions in forthcoming supplement. Final
                    recommendation based on current status decrees will be sent you by telegram to
                    arrive Washington not later Monday afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
